course: dictionary
lesson: 5840
title: One word, many meanings: makeup
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Makeup is a good example. Most people think of face paint, such as lipstick and mascara, but the words around the word show you which meaning is meant.
explain: «A mineral is a natural solid with a fixed chemical makeup and atoms arranged in a regular pattern.» The clues are chemical and atoms. This is a science sentence, so makeup does not mean face paint. It means what something is made of.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. «A mineral has a fixed chemical makeup» becomes «A mineral has a fixed chemical what it is made of.» That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Always check the clues before you decide.
fact: Makeup (noun) can mean coloured creams and powders for the face, such as lipstick, mascara and foundation.
fact: The makeup of something is what it is made of, or the parts in it: «the makeup of the air».
fact: A person's makeup is their character, the way they are.
fact: In US schools, a makeup test is one you take later because you missed the first one.
fact: Makeup is also written as make-up or make-up, and in the UK a make-up is usually the face paint.
exercise: «A mineral is a natural solid with a fixed chemical makeup and atoms arranged in a regular pattern.» What does makeup mean here? | *What something is made of | A test taken later | Face paint like lipstick | A type of rock
exercise: Lena says makeup in a science text means face paint. Why is she wrong? | Science texts never use words with more than one meaning | *Words like chemical and atoms show it means what something is made of | Face paint is always chemical | Atoms are a kind of face paint
exercise: Which word in «A mineral is a natural solid with a fixed chemical makeup» is the clue that this is a science sentence? | Mascara | Lipstick | Foundation | *Chemical
test: «The makeup of the air is about 78% nitrogen.» What does makeup mean here? | A test taken later | Stage makeup | Face paint | *The parts that something is made of
test: In a US school, Sam says he has a makeup on Friday. What does makeup mean? | The parts that something is made of | Coloured creams for the face | *A test taken later, because he missed the first one | A character
exam: Which meaning fits «He put on makeup before the show»? | A test taken later | *Coloured creams and powders for the face | The parts that something is made of | A type of rock
